@startuml sc11-asset-install
title Use Case 5, Scenario 11 — asset installation and removal updates\nMMS publishes to O&M systems

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 12

actor "Maintenance technician" as TechUser
actor "Maintenance planner" as PlannerUser
actor "Condition monitoring engineer" as RelUser

box "SimHost — simulated participants"
  participant "MMS" as MMS
  participant "CMS" as OM
end box

participant "ws-ISBM provider" as ISBM

' Scenario 10 would place an I&C Device Monitoring System here, sensing the
' physical change and giving MMS an independent confirmation to reconcile
' against. It is deliberately out of scope, so everything below rests on the
' technician's word alone.

== Precondition ==

note over MMS
  The functional location already exists in MMS,
  provisioned by Use Case 1. Use Case 5 assumes
  it; it does not create it.
end note

== The physical work ==

TechUser -> MMS : complete WO-40001\ninstalled SN-88213 at P-101
activate MMS
MMS -> MMS : record OccurredAt = time of work,\nnot time of entry
note right of MMS
  The order is often keyed days after the fact.
  A receiver that timestamped on arrival would
  be wrong by the length of that delay, and every
  time-in-service figure built on it with them.
end note
MMS --> TechUser : work order completed
deactivate MMS

== Release event: planner sign-off ==

PlannerUser -> MMS : sign off WO-40001
activate MMS
MMS -> MMS : commit EquipmentRecord.FunctionalLocation\n+ WorkOrder.SignedOff + Outbox row\n(single transaction)
note right of MMS
  Sign-off publishes, completion does not.
  Publishing on completion would broadcast
  work the planner may still reject.
end note
MMS --> PlannerUser : signed off
deactivate MMS

== Publication ==

MMS -> ISBM : OpenPublicationSession(/Enterprise/Site/OandM-Events)
activate ISBM
ISBM --> MMS : sessionId
MMS -> ISBM : PostPublication(SyncAssetSegmentEvents)\ntopic = AssetSegmentEvents
deactivate ISBM

note over MMS, OM
  Publication only. No response, no acknowledgement,
  no human gate on the receiving side — unlike the
  as-built handover, nobody is being asked to accept
  anything. The event already happened.
end note

ISBM -> OM : ReadPublication
activate OM
OM -> OM : record AssetInstallationEvent\nEventType = ecc99353-… (installation)
OM -> OM : Cirid = NULL
note right of OM
  It cannot say what the asset is. No registry has
  reconciled the identifier and CMS holds
  no reference data, so the gap is left visible
  rather than filled with a guess.
end note
deactivate OM

== Removal, six months later ==

TechUser -> MMS : complete WO-40002\nremoved SN-88213 for bearing failure
activate MMS
PlannerUser -> MMS : sign off WO-40002
MMS -> MMS : EquipmentRecord.FunctionalLocation = NULL\n(in the workshop, installed nowhere)
MMS -> ISBM : PostPublication(SyncAssetSegmentEvents)\nEventType = 3a45e126-… (removal)
deactivate MMS

ISBM -> OM : ReadPublication
activate OM
OM -> OM : append second AssetInstallationEvent
note right of OM
  Appended, not overwritten. A "currently installed"
  field would now say the pump was never there, and
  the six-month service interval — the only thing a
  condition monitoring system wanted from this feed — would
  be unrecoverable.
end note
deactivate OM

RelUser -> OM : open SN-88213
activate OM
OM --> RelUser : install and removal both present\nservice interval computable
deactivate OM

@enduml
